{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"confused-episodic-rat","creation_channel":"cli","description":"Update the author-facing documentation so writers know to de-risk risky runtime mechanisms out-of-loop before committing them to a slow delivery loop — the behavior T15 rewards.\n\n## Work\n- src/rebar/_guides/writing-a-passing-plan.md (surfaced by `rebar explain plan`): add guidance that when a plan stands up work whose correctness only resolves after a slow codified delivery loop (CI/CD, IaC apply, provisioning), the plan should name the risky mechanism(s) and commit to a concrete fast out-of-loop proof (a local run OR a manual probe against the real target) before codifying — and that throwaway experiments must be cleaned up scoped to only what they created.\n- docs/plan-review-gate.md: if it enumerates the overlay criteria, add a one-line pointer to T15 (the generated docs/plan-review-criteria-guide.md is updated by the criterion child, not here).\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n- `rebar explain plan` output includes the de-risk-before-the-slow-loop guidance with the local-or-manual-proof phrasing.\n- Any hand-authored gate doc that lists overlays references T15 consistently with the generated guide.\n- Guidance uses stack-agnostic language (no hardcoded Terraform/docker).","id":"3192-a652-0368-42c2","parent_id":"8fc2-0306-a9a0-4864","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"task","title":"Update writing-a-passing-plan guide + gate docs for de-risk-before-slow-loop"},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1784918875620810001,"uuid":"6d834553-0e31-48c0-b1e3-90faa84cc699"}